OL,3,GNEWSAHow major policy shift is changing
OL,4,Apolice response to mental health
OL,5,Acall-outs
OL,6,
OL,7,FPolice in Northern Ireland handle
OL,8,F30,000 mental health calls every year,
OL,9,For about 80 a day on average - but a
OL,10,Fmajor new policy will see a significant
OL,11,Fchange in how those calls are answered.
OL,13,FFrom the start of November, the Police
OL,14,FService of Northern Ireland (PSNI) will
OL,15,Fno longer carry out concern-for-welfare
OL,16,Fchecks unless there's a risk to life or
OL,17,Fharm or a crime involved.
OL,19,FThe public will still phone 999, but
OL,20,Fcalls will be assessed and handlers may
OL,21,Fpass them onto other emergency services
OL,22,For health and social care staff.
OL,23,APub: 30-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,415,410,260,120,0,100
